  "actualContracts": [
    "Untouched /3 audit is genuinely Ed25519-signed through the current binder signer and trusted only under the independently pre-recorded artifact-seal pin; independent node:crypto verification confirms signature bytes.",
    "A coherent B-workspace signature and B-binder-signed attacker replacement envelope pass actual integrity but remain untrusted under A-only context. Independently recorded B trust positively verifies both exact controls.",
    "All strict/allow-unpinned/allow-unanchored/both variants preserve trusted:false for foreign and attacker issuers; allow-unpinned returns integrity-only exit2, not trusted or exit0. Other cases return refusal1.",
    "Explicit public PEM and embedded key alone are locator candidates and do not confer issuer admission.",
    "Meaningful first control ADEQUATE/L3\u2192PASS/L5 tamper plus recomputed checksum preserves the original signature, passes checksum and fails current digest/signature checks.",
    "Unsigned bundles are refused1 under all four allow variants. Actual no-answer baseline has overall.claimKind synthetic_example, null eligibleLevel and cannot be signed. Bad checksums are also refused by the signer.",
    "All20 answered signed/control verifier outputs and signed/unsigned L3/L5 controls remain self_reported/not_evaluated with eligibleLevel1. Markdown canonical labels preserve those caps; verifier trust does not promote answer claims."
  ],
